Track 3: Adunni’s Communal Mortar
- Story & Context: Named after the archive's decommissioned cafeteria where the night crew gathered to share starch and palm oil after twelve-hour preservation shifts, this sprawling ten-minute instrumental became folklore among the bunker staff when the building was abandoned. The track centers on the deep, wooden thud of a heavy yam mortar recorded in the hall's cavernous tile acoustics, intertwined with muted talking-drum murmurs and double vibraphones that spiral upward into gossamer vocal clouds until the line breaks into soft laughter: "The jar stays shut, but the music leaks out." It serves as the scene’s parting myth, proving that communal warmth could sprout inside thirty feet of permafrost.
